  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The paper uses atomic-resolution electron tomography to reconstruct three-dimensional atomic coordinates of gold–palladium five-fold twinned icosahedral nanoparticles and investigate how intrinsic angular deficiency and strain are relieved through a Janus-like mechanism involving edge dislocations and amorphization that enlarge solid angles of selected tetrahedra on one hemisphere while the opposite hemisphere remains nearly ideal fcc.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
